d like we're  not even gonna tell them  that friday afternoon special needs  teacher shane batuyan  is put on leave with pay pending an  investigation communications tells the  principal to let the parents know that  petuyon's on leave  on monday school police are a no-show  but cps shows up to the school  officers arrive at the school tuesday  afternoon  six days after concerns were first  reported police begin an investigation  barnett says she first learned about the  investigation from  cps not from school leaders or police  it made me panic i'm at home i just sent  my kid to the war zone he's  being abused police say battulion denied  hitting the children but he said he told  them the stick was a magic wand to give  them powers and it was a secret  detectives concluded that six students  were hit tapped or poked  and recommended charges be filed against  him for six counts of battery  two other parents maria garcia and larry  bracamontes say they were not  told their children were identified as  victims by police  until barnett's lawyers contacted them a  year later  what i want is the ccnc take  responsibility  to be held accountable because  they knew garcia's daughter is  considered non-verbal  petuyen's aide told police he told her  to take students to another classroom  every day garcia is concerned she  doesn't know about what may have  happened if her daughter was alone with  him  that we take our children to school  thinking they're going to be  safe and they're not the three families  have filed a federal lawsuit against  ccsd the principal and assistant  principal the aide and batuyan  a relative of petullians tells the  i-team he believes he's in the  philippines  we discovered he still has a nevada  teaching license  a spokeswoman for the department of  education tells the i-team the  department  recently learned about allegations and  will investigate  by law ccsd is required to report  aversive intervention against  children with disabilities incl